# Documentation

## Do

- Create or edit `.md` / README / skills only when the user asks, or when the task explicitly includes docs.
- Write `.cursor/` docs (rules, skills) in English.
- Use a short H1, then H2/H3 without skipped levels.
- Prefer short Must lists and tables over long prose.
- Fence code with a language tag (`ts`, `tsx`, `scss`).
- Link skills/rules with relative paths when useful.

## Cursor rules (`.mdc`)

- Keep one concern per file; aim for 50-80 lines of body.
- Set frontmatter `description` plus `globs` and/or `alwaysApply`.
- Prefer good/bad examples over abstract wording.
- Point to a skill for depth; keep the rule as Must only.

## Avoid

- Do not generate project overviews or tutorial markdown unprompted.
- Do not paste secrets, tokens, or `.env` values into docs.

## Example frontmatter

```yaml
---
description: "Noun phrase describing the rule"
globs: project/src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
```
